a sharp warning from the white house  tonight that a russian invasion of  ukraine could happen at any moment  canada joined several other nations  today urging its citizens to leave  ukraine now top u.s security officials  have laid out what a russian attack  could look like starting with an aerial  bombing campaign  jackson proskow joins us now from  washington jackson what more do we know  tonight  hi eric the white house insists that it  does not believe vladimir putin has made  a final decision on an invasion but the  tone today was unmistakable president  biden's national security adviser told  reporters that russia is in position to  mount a major military campaign any day  now and it could happen while the  olympics are still ongoing in addition  to urging americans to leave within the  next 24 to 48 hours they warned no u.s  military personnel will step onto  ukrainian soil to assist with evacuating  citizens in the event of an invasion the  u.s embassy continues its drawdown of  staff and there is growing concern that  a bloody assault beginning with missiles  and air strikes and bombings could be  the first salvo in any russian attack it  could take a range of different forms  but i want to be equally clear that one  of those forms  is a rapid assault on the city of kiev  that is a possible  line of attack course of action that the  russian forces could choose to take now  tonight we're learning that the u.s is  ordering an additional 3 000 troops to  poland that's on top of the nearly 2 000  dispatch there last week they are not  meant to fight russia in ukraine but  rather to deter any advance on nato  members today there was an 80-minute  long phone call between the u.s canada  and european allies the white house  insists they're all united and ready to  levy sanctions and other countermeasures  against vladimir putin and his inner  circle if needed but eric officially  they aren't giving up on diplomacy yet  and the white house expects that  president biden will speak with putin by  phone this weekend  thanks jackson jackson proskow in  washington tonight
 

